hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"80","On supplication. Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Ali ibn Abi Talib, who had gone out for the Fajr prayer, while Ali was saying: O Allah, forgive me; O Allah, have mercy on me; O Allah, accept my repentance. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his shoulder and said to him: Generalize - for the merit of the general over the particular is like that between heaven and earth."
"81","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah and Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Abdullah ibn Bujayr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never heard one praising Allah, Mighty and Majestic, without prolonging the praise with him. Humayd said in his narration: Bishr narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Bujayr ibn Humran al-Qaysi narrated to us."
